{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And Sarai was barren; she had no child.</b> There are women who remain a long time barren and afterward have children. Scripture informed that she was barren and added ״she had no child,״ meaning that it was not in her nature ever to have a child. And therefore they both agreed — Avram and Sarai — to depart from there and go to the land of Canaan; perhaps by the merit of the Holy Land they would build a family there. And even though Scripture says ״and Terach took,״ it is known that Avram was the principal; but because Avram honored his father and followed him, setting him as master over his entire household, it says ״and Terach took,״ as though Terach were the principal — for those going with them were Sarai and Lot. <b>And it is known</b> that for Avram's sake they went, not for Terach's sake; and so we find with Lot, that even after Terach's death he went with Avram."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:11:41.771843442Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}